<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n475" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγέρ-ωχος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, poet. Adj. (used also in late Prose,
		v. infr.), in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> always in good sense, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>high-minded, lordly</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρῶες,
				Ῥόδιοι, Μυσοί</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.654
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.430
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				122
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				5.35
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάτραχοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Batr.
					145
				</span></i>
			; once of a single man, viz. Periclymenus, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.286
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				14
			</span></i>; of <i>noble</i> actions, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἕργματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					6.34
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νίκη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>O.</u>
					10(11).79
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλούτου στεφάνωμ᾽ ἀ</span>.
				<i>lordly</i> crown of wealth, <i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				1.50
			</span></i>; <i>high-spirited</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				2.2
			</span></i>,al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγέρωχα σκιρτᾶν</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				32
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότερα γυμνάσια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Gym.</u>
					46
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later in bad
			sense, <i>arrogant</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				154
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				120
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				162
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>3 Ma.</u>
				1.25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὄνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Asin.</u>
					40
				</span></i>
			; of things, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυτόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Anacreont.</u>
					53.42
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-χως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.745
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Anyte</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.8.7
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					18.34.3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
